            <ArticleTitle>Giant calcified pseudoaneurysm of right coronary artery presenting as a right intra-atrial mass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>969-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2009.06.121</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a giant right coronary artery pseudoaneurysm that presented as a right atrial intracardiac mass. Preoperatively, a two-dimensional echocardiogram, a computed tomographic scan, a magnetic resonance image, and cardiac catheterization were performed to diagnose and assess the origins of the mass.</AbstractText>
